        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I wrote `{\"invariant_exists\": false}` to the answer file. I didn't open the test file or `keras/src/optimizers/adam.py`, so this rests on how AMSGrad normally works, not on reading this repo's code.\n\n- **Why it's false:** In AMSGrad, `v_hat` is updated as `max(v_hat, v)`. So it never goes down, but it only goes up when the new second-moment estimate `v` is higher than the old maximum.\n- **When it stays flat:** If a gradient coordinate is zero or getting smaller, `v` drops below `v_hat` and `v_hat` stays exactly the same. That breaks \"strictly increasing at every step\". A test class with \"diverse gradient sequences\" almost certainly includes such cases.\n- **Supporting hint:** The test file's name ends in `_strict_increase_false_test.py`, which points the same way.",
